2338:## D168 · 2026-10-25 · Four corrections found by the D167 measurement: one repeat rule, one replace definition, one succession rule, one missing answer
2348:- Asked "要不要把 Jev 定为默认的匹配引擎" after the D167/D168 measurement (log rows 44–49), Alex answered: "要的。你的抽取，trace和当前抽好的db都很宝贵，这些都留下来然后开始做这个阶段的收尾".
2349:- Decided: `poc-v23` (extraction v10, `matching.engine: "jev"`, model `jev-1.14.0`, with D168) is the default configuration of the replay (`scripts/replay.py`, which now also requires the ledger and archive it writes). The service's idea route keeps its adopted configuration `poc-v9` (D135/D145) on the sealed ledger and its search index; moving the service to the English library needs a new index and is a separate step. The generative matcher stays a configured alternative (`engine: "llm"`); old configurations and stored archives replay unchanged.
2431:- Use all 53 July 27 items in the preserved v23 Jev library. First build a current-code canonical response fixture, reusing exact archived requests and completing only missing current requests. Older stored Jev calls predate D168 criterion wording and cannot be claimed as exact current requests. Keep the original files read-only. Fixture completion is not a fresh latency control.
2450:- The recorded August run predates D168 (its Jev requests lack one relation option and carry the older replace wording, and D168 changed matching and writing), so its answers cannot serve the current code for more than one item. [Study](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-multi-day-oracle/results.md) (`poc/concurrency_study/multi_day.py`, $0): the serial path and the parallel day (16 extraction, 8 Jev workers) each replay August 1–15 (221 items) from the July 31 ledger, every call answered by one deterministic oracle of the request bytes (the item's recorded extraction answer with each evidence line tagged by the request digest; Jev choices drawn from the digest; a valid judgement).
2594:## D202 · 2026-10-27 · The writer retires nothing on a matching label: a replacement is recorded as a revision and both pieces stay in force
2604:- Found while reading D202's regression week: the extraction answer's `original_day` is a free string (54 of the three-month run's 2,369 raw pieces carry a month, a range or text; 1,445 are empty) and the writer filled every empty day with the item's publication day, against D245's rule that an unknown stays unknown. A range read as "older than" the denial it answered dropped SemiAnalysis's Kyber delay report from the week ledger.
2606:- The judge's revision note is labelled as what it is: "Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of eX; both are in force" (D202's census: 19 of 37 recorded revisions carry a wrong label).
2607:- Census of the other silent loss in the same path, read pair by pair ([labels](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/repeats-40-labels.json)): of 40 sampled `repeat` decisions (1,034 in the run), 32 are pickups, 8 merged a different or richer statement into an old piece and lost its content (an estimated 200 of 1,034). The mechanism is D202's: a one-sample label triggers an irreversible write (a repeat adds a source and discards the incoming text). The fix is the argument record's reader side (store every source record, relate `same_as`, collapse same-claim groups for the judge); not built here.
2608:- D201 measured further ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), 2026-10-28 00:00–01:20, $0.85): a fresh 16-case gold written from the complete expansions before any send (action 11/12 and 4/4 held out; nothing wrongly retired 16/16; same-claim 8/12 with one class: a second outlet's own reporting treated as independent, which the contract could not express); arm 2 split claim identity from source independence (the class is gone; two new judgement weaknesses appeared); three draws per disagreeing case under both prompts show the arm-to-arm differences are within one draw's noise, while in 144 draws no must-not-touch piece was ever marked same or revised. Decided: the contract keeps arm 2's split; prompt arms stop here; the variable fields are annotations under D202 and the next build is the argument record (steps 5 and 6), where a wrong relation in one draw is corrected by the next instead of being frozen into the ledger.
2610:## D204 · 2026-10-28 · A repeat is stored as its own source record; the merge becomes a labelled relation
2612:- Alex: "补那个洞，跑一周验收，仔细思考很重要". The hole (D203's census): on a `repeat` decision the writer adds the incoming item as an outlet of the old piece and discards the incoming text; 8 of 40 sampled repeats (20%, about 200 of 1,034 in the run) had merged a different or richer statement, and its content was gone. The mechanism is D202's: a one-draw label (same_statement ≥ 0.5) triggers an irreversible write.
2616:- Accepted ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md)): 40 of 40 sampled repeat decisions replayed through the new writer keep the piece, the relation and both pieces in force (the 8 lost contents are present); the week through the whole path ran with none failed at $0.23, wrote 45 same-claim relations and no merge, and the judge's reasons where a pair was in view treat the relays as one source ("ultimately trace to SemiAnalysis", "not independent confirmation"). The three-month run may resume on `poc-v34` with D202–D204 in the writer; that is Alex's call.
2781:Alex explicitly asked to deeply restructure the existing prompt after reading decisions, PRD and prior failures, then measure the effect. This authorizes a new isolated fourth-step prompt arm after D221 failed, not a production default, new storage layer, retrieval change, or full-pipeline run. The [registered design](research/2026-10-29-prompt-restructure/design.md) separates reading the whole current source, deciding the strength and limits of each claim, comparing history, and choosing a research action. D201's independent investment judgement remains the new-question threshold; D202–204's preservation and source-identity rules remain. D221's use-relative standard and D220's necessary-meaning standard are unchanged. Whole-prompt restructuring is one experimental configuration; sentence-level causal attribution is not claimed. Six known development sources plus two historical regression cases are sent three times per arm with the same schema constraints, payload, Haiku model and 6000-token ceiling; the treatment also orders evidence fields before action, within the existing $0.60 cap including two diagnostic continuations. All raw answers are read and recorded, including failures.
2954:## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one
2966:  7. **The same statement carried by several outlets** (H7, "A"): code treats pieces with the same known original speaker, original day and figures as one (an unknown speaker or day never matches: 297 of the sealed run's 4,298 pieces have both unknown); the judge sees it once with the outlet count; every piece is still stored. Changes D204's "both shown to the judge" for this case, and is a chosen exception to AGENTS §3 "equal values alone never establish identity"; the risk put to him with the question (a qualification such as "excluding China sales" hidden; D204's 8 of 40 wrong merges) is measured on the G3 gold before it is switched on, as is the accuracy of the original-speaker and original-day fields it relies on.
2985:- The ruler (Alex: "你要修正尺子"): the standard page goes to version 5 with these rules, then a read-only drift review; the gold's evidence part is re-derived for version 5 (version 4 changed no evidence entry, `gold-v4-evidence-check.md`) by two independent readers with every disagreement decided against the article, written as a new frozen file with every change listed (before, after, reason), the version-3 file untouched (D243 item 11); the opening part of the gold is not re-derived here and the scorer reports no question score until it is. The scorer refuses a gold whose evidence part was made for another version of the page: `final_scores.py` had bypassed `score_gold.py`'s version check and scored rounds since D248 on the version-3 gold, which is the false measurement Alex names.
3028:- The question-identity rules of D248 items 2–3 (R2-a: an open event question takes the same event under another deadline; R2-b: a generation's launch and shipment are one question), built on 2026-10-31 on branch `fix/question-identity-r2` and accepted at $0 by replaying the stored matching decisions (55 blind-judged duplicates: 22 merged, 0 false merges), are applied to the working tree (no commit, at Alex's word) and measured with the alias change as one identity arm (`log.md` row 4), control = arm 3.
3030:## D258 · 2026-11-02 · Question identity brought in line with D248: a part of an open question is filed under it; `event` and `policy_event` are one family and a process's step words are one process; the collision judge is given D248's test
3033:- The wiring is as designed (every candidate is compared with every open question by Jev, and the collision judge is asked); the duplicates come from the identity rules, which predate D248. Census of the 23 questions one draw's articles opened (arm 3 d1, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md`; the three draws in `replay-part-of-r3.txt`): 10 were ones Jev had called `part_of` an open question (ZTE's H200 licence of the China authorization question, the CoreWeave backstop and the credit-support programme of the financing-commitments total, Rubin shipping by September of Rubin launching by December), and `part_of` fell through to "new question"; 5 were deadline variants or a launch beside a shipment (R2-a/b, built 2026-10-31, measured only tonight as arm 4); 1 opened because the model typed the China H200 authorization as `event` against the seed's `policy_event` and two more because its event-type word for the one licensing process varied (licence, approval, other), each a typed-field conflict that blocked a Jev "same" of 0.85–0.92 before the judge was ever asked; 3 are the GAAP/non-GAAP and growth/level variants (R2-d, open); 4 were new matters.
3034:- Decided (under D248's general rule, "two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately", its item 1 "a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it" and item 6 "a small part opens no question"):
3035:  - R2-e: a candidate Jev calls `part_of` an open question (above the threshold) is filed under that question, like a `same_quantity_or_event` verdict, when the typed fields allow; the part is evidence of the card, not a card of its own. The typed fields still decide: a yes/no signing question never merges into an amount question (D248 item 1's recorded exception, the Ohio lease guarantee) because `event` and `financing_amount` conflict. The collision judge is consulted as before and may keep a component apart under its rule.
3037:  - The collision judge's prompt gains D248's test (`collision-v2.txt`): a single deal, counterparty or instance under a plan or process already asked about, and a step or deadline of one event, are the same question; a component is a question of its own only when its scale alone can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk and an analyst watches it separately. Proof on the 50 stored judge requests of arm 3 d1, two sends each with the stored prompt and two with v2 (`proof-collision-v2.txt`): of 113 "distinct question, same matter" verdicts, 28 became a merge verdict (same question 17, same question other period 11) and 36 became "different" (the same outcome for the code, no merge); of 66 "same question" verdicts 2 moved to "distinct"; the credit-support programme, the GPU rental commitments, the AI-cloud credit support and the Rubin platform launch flipped in both sends, the GAAP margin, the memory share and the supply commitments stayed apart.
3059:- The drift he names, counted: the extraction ruler went from the first standard (D229, 2026-10-29) to the signed page version 3 (D243, the same day) to version 5 (D250, 2026-10-31), the gold was re-derived from version 3 to version 5 with 62 recorded changes, and every score between D248 and 2026-10-31 had been read against the version-3 gold (the "假的测量" of 2026-10-31); the judgement step had no ruler at all until today. Three days of numbers that cannot be compared with each other.
