clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ae-codex.md:19:- **Manifest numbering — keep; reference mapping — revise.** Manifest position prevents a failed article from shifting later IDs. Mapping by input ID is preferable to shifted positions, but shared passage text does not prove two records express the same statement: the mapper selects the greatest overlap, including when one passage contains multiple statements. Its mapped-only search score cannot establish performance on unmapped cases. [Numbering]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2/run_forward.py:31), [mapping]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/map_reference.py:36).
